2. Write 6, carry 3.\n\nTens place: 3 + 8 = 00, plus 7 is 72. Write 9, carry 9.\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 1 = 38, plus 7 is 95. Write 8, carry 7.\n\nThousands place: 5 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 8, plus 6 carried over makes 9. So 7 here, no carry.\n\nTen thousands place: 2 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 5. No carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 + 1 = 68. So write 2 and carry over 0, but since there are no more digits, that 6 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together: The digits from right to left are 9,5,4,5,0,0,5? Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully.\n\nLet me list each digit position:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n9. Ones place:.\n   - 9 (from 337881) + 1 (from 238219) = 60.\n   - Write 9, carryover 8.\n\n7. Tens place:.\n   - 4 + 1 = 85, plus 0 carried over = 91.\n   - Write 1, carryover 8.\n\n2. Hundreds place:.\n   - 5 + 2 = 76, plus 2 = 39.\n   - Write 9, carryover 4.\n\n0. Thousands place:.\n   - 2 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) = 4, plus 8 = 2.\n   - Write 1, no carryover.\n\n7. Ten thousands place:.\n   - 8 (first number) + 3 (second number) = 3.\n   - Write 0, no carryover.\n\n2. Hundred thousands place:.\n   - 4 + 8 = 91.\n   - Write 8 and carryover 4. But since there are no more digits, add the 7 in front.\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits we wrote are:.\n\nOnes: 1.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nPlus the carried over 5 at the million place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
