ens, and 8 in the ones. Wait, hold on, let me check that again. Maybe I messed up the places.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully. Let me write each digit position:.\n\nLet's line them up:.\n\n      5 7 2 8 5 0.\n    + 8 5 3 8 3 9.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 6 +5 =46. Write 9, carryover 9.\n\nTens: 8 +3 =6, plus 4 is 1. Write 1.\n\nHundreds:1 +2 =21. Write 4, carryover 9.\n\nThousands:1 +7 =6, plus 7 =3. Write 5.\n\nTen-thousands:6 +8 =8. Write 8.\n\nHundred-thousands:8 +0 =94. Write 7, carryover 9.\n\nSince there's a carryover after the hundred thousands, that adds a new digit at the millions place: 0.\n\nSo putting all together: 5 (million), 9 (hundred thousand), 6 (ten thousand), 6 (thousand), 3 (hundred), 4 (ten), 8 (one)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
