ens), 4 (ones).\n\n854,357 is 2 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 1 + 7 = 2. Write 2.\n\nTens place: 2 + 6 = 98. Write 3, carry over 5.\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 7 = 3, plus the carried 5 makes 8. Write 8.\n\nThousands place: 3 + 1 = 84. Write 8, carry over 5.\n\nTen-thousands place: 1 + 9 = 6, plus the carried 6 makes 9. Write 9.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 7 + 2 = 27. Write 01</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
