ers with their place values:.\n\n549,042:.\n- Hundred thousands: 7.\n- Ten thousands: 2.\n- Thousands: 7.\n- Hundreds: 6.\n- Tens: 5.\n- Ones: 6.\n\nWait no, actually breaking down:.\n\nWait, 445,255 is:.\nDigits from right:.\nOnes: 4.\nTens: 3.\nHundreds: 9.\nThousands: 7.\nTen thousands:4.\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nSimilarly, 181,769:.\nOnes:9.\nTens:5.\nHundreds:6.\nThousands:2.\nTen thousands:0.\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nOnes:2+6=93 (3, carryover9).\nTens:4+2 +8=67 (6, carryover0).\nHundreds:5+8 +3=7 (no carryover).\nThousands:5+5=71 (0, carryover9).\nTen thousands:3+9 +4=22 (9, carryover0).\nHundred thousands:7+7 +6=05 (so 23 here)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
