Starting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\n4 (from 987317) + 9 (from 226580) = 27. Write 9, carryover 6.\n\nTens place:.\n4 + 2 = 23, plus the 7 carried over is 62. Write 4, carryover 9.\n\nHundreds place:.\n7 +8 =6, plus 7 is 39. Write 7, carryover 9.\n\nThousands place:.\n4 +1 =4, plus 4 is 9. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:.\n9 (from first number) +0 (from second number) =82. Write 7, carryover 6.\n\nHundred thousands place:.\n4 +5 =07, plus the 3 carried over is 80. Write 7 and carryover 7.\n\nMillions place: The carryover 6. Since both numbers don't have millions digits beyond that, so the total is 8,6 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nWait, so putting all digits together: 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
