digit, the sum might be a seven-digit number here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, actually, let me go through each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nAligning the numbers:.\n\n```.\n  827897.\n+ 703875.\n----------.\n```.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 7 = 5 ✔️.\n\nTens: 2 + 5 = 1 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 9 = 1 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 8 + 0 = 0 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands: 2 (from first number) + 6 (from second) = 84. So write 3, carry over 0. ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands: 7 + 9 = 1, plus the carried 6 makes 44. So yes, that's 92. So the hundred thousands place becomes 6, and we have to carry over 6 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that carried 5 becomes the new digit in the millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
