gher place, that 8 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\nOnes: 6.\nTens: 3.\nHundreds: 7.\nThousands: 8 (with a carry-over).\nTen-thousands: 7 (with a carry-over).\nHundred-thousands: 5 (plus the carry-over gives 51, so 7 here and carry-over 0).\nMillions place: 4 (from the carry-over)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
