um of 458,150.\n\nI think that's all. Let me just make sure there's no arithmetic mistake here.\n\nDouble-checking:\n\n121,829\n\n+336,321\n\nAdding the units digits: 9+1=10 (0 with carry 1)\n\nTens: 2+2=4 +1=5\n\nHundreds:8+3=11 (1, carry 1)\n\nThousands:1 (from first number's thousands place) +6 (second number's thousands place) is 7+1=8.\n\nTen thousands: 2 +3 =5.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +3=4.\n\nYes, so the result is indeed 458,150. Alright, I think that's solid.\n</think>", ''] 14%|#4        | 71/500 [1:25:28<13:50:12, 116.11s/it]
