Putting all together: 12 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (ones). So that's 1,240,315?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Let's add 826,198 + 414,117.\n\nFirst, 800,000 + 400,000 = 1,200,000\n\nThen 26,000 +14,000 = 40,000 \u2192 total so far 1,240,000\n\nThen 198 +117 = 315. Adding that gives 1,240,315. Okay, that matches.\n\nSo the correct answer should be 1,240,315. Wait, but in my first attempt, I had messed up the numbers, but after correcting, it's 1,240,315. Let me make sure the digit-by-digit addition was done correctly.\n\nYes, step by step:\n\nOnes: 8+7=15 \u2192 5, carry 1.\n\nTens:9+1=10 +1=11 \u2192 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:1+1=2 +1=3 \u2192 3, no carry.\n\nThousands:6+4=10 \u2192 0, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 (from 826k) +1 (from 414k) =3, plus the carried 1 makes 4.\n\nHundred-thousands:8+4=12.\n\nSo combining all digits: 12 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens),5 (ones). So 1,240,315. That's correct.\n\nSo the answer is 1,240,315. I need to present this in the template. Let me structure the reasoning properly.\n\nFirst, align the numbers:\n\n  826198\n\n+414117\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n1. Ones place: 8 + 7 = 15. Write down 5, carry over 1.\n\n2. Tens place: 9 + 1 = 10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. Write 1, carry over 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 1 + 1 = 2, plus the carried 1 equals 3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\n4. Thousands place: 6 + 4 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1.\n\n5. Ten-thousands place: 2 + 1 = 3, plus the carried 1 gives 4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\n6. Hundred-thousands place: 8 + 4 = 12. Write 12.\n\nCombining all digits from right to left: 12 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (ones). So the total is 1,240,315.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me confirm with another method: 826,198 + 400,000 = 1,226,198. Then add the remaining 14,117 (since 414,117 is 400k +14,117). So 1,226,198 +14,117 = 1,240,315. Yes, that's the same. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
