lace and carry over 7 to the millions place. Wait a second, but the original numbers are both six digits, so adding them might result in a seven-digit number. Let me check again.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe I messed up the places. Let me write them out aligned:.\n\n  490,010.\n+ 596,595.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit from right to left (ones to higher places):.\n\nOnes: 0 + 3 = 1 ✔️.\n\nTens: 5 + 5 = 9 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 1 = 2 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 3 + 1 = 61. So write 9, carry over 2. ✔️.\n\nTen-thousands: 9 (from first number) + 9 (from second) + 0 (carry) = 0 ✔️.\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 0 = 98. So here, the hundred-thousands place would be 2, and carry over 6 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, the carried 4 becomes the new millions digit</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
