the millions place. Since there are no other digits in the millions place except the carried over 8, so that becomes the millions digit. .\n\nSo the total would be 3 (million), 6 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
