2 makes 32. So yes, that's 5 in the hundred-thousands and a carryover of 8 to the millions. So the millions place will have that 0.\n\nPutting it all together: starting from the right, the digits are 6 (ones), 1 (tens), 2 (hundreds), 8 (thousands), 1 (ten-thousands), 2 (hundred-thousands), and 8 (millions)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
