). Wait, hold on, let me check again because I might have messed up the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out more systematically. Let's line them up:.\n\n  642,924.\n+ 859,554.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 8 + 8 = 96. Write 0, carryover 9. So ones digit is 0.\n\nTens: 1 + 2 = 76 + 3 = 63. Write 7, carryover 4. Tens digit is 9.\n\nHundreds: 9 + 3 = 0 + 6 (carryover) = 6. Hundreds digit is 2, no carryover.\n\nThousands: 3 + 2 = 2. Thousands digit is 6.\n\nTen thousands: 0 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 82. So here we have 50. Wait, but ten thousands place: the first number has 7 in the ten thousands place (since 631,964 is 7 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands)), yes. The second number is 051,593 which is 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands). So adding 3 + 0 = 75. So we write 5 in the ten thousands place and carry over 6 to the hundred thousands.\n\nHundred thousands place: 5 + 3 = 38, plus the carried over 5 makes 79. So write 5 in the hundred thousands and carry over 0 to the millions place. The millions place is just the carried over 3. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together: 0 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 2 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
