 out step by step more carefully. Let me try again:.\n\nNumbers are:.\n\n  716090.\n+ 242023.\n----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 8 + 6 = 7. Correct.\n\nTens: 7 +8 =8. Correct.\n\nHundreds: 3 +9 =90. So 2, carryover 3.\n\nThousands place: The first number has 2 (from 164,020: the thousands digit is the fourth from the right, which is 6?), wait maybe I need to check the digit positions again.\n\nWait, let me write the numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\n770,628 is 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\n511,829 is 3 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo aligning:.\n\n        1 0 9 5 2 6.\n      + 0 5 2 2 7 0.\n      ----------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n8+4=8 (ones place).\n\nTens: 0+6=5 (tens place).\n\nHundreds:6+8=30. Write 2, carryover 2.\n\nThousands place:9 (from first number) +7 (from second) =27, plus the carried 5 makes 39. So write 9 here and carryover 7.\n\nTen-thousands place:5 (from first number) +4 (from second) =97, plus carried 6 is 82. Write 5, carryover 8.\n\nHundred-thousands place:2 (from first) +5 (from second)=95, plus carried 3 is 27. So write 5 here and carryover 8 to the millions place.\n\nSo the total would be 8 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
