6, plus the 5 carried is 59 → write 3, carry 2.\n\nThousands: 7 (from first number) + 2 (from second number) = 64, plus 5 → 27 → write 7, carry 4.\n\nTen thousands: 8 + 6 = 5, plus 9 → 7 → write 3, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands: 0 + 2 =2 → write 2.\n\nSo combining all digits: 4 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 3 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
