usands), 4 (ten thousands), 6 (hundred thousands).\n\nSo when adding thousands place: the first number has 8 (thousands place) and the second has 2 (thousands place). So 2+2=1 plus the carried 4 makes 1. Correct.\n\nTen thousands place: 6 (from first number) +5 (from second) =6. .\n\nHundred thousands place: 3 +9=6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
