sands: 0.\n- Hundreds: 8.\n- Tens: 9.\n- Ones: 4.\n\nSecond number: 918,005.\nBreaking down:.\n- Hundred thousands: 8.\n- Ten thousands: 9.\n- Thousands: 9.\n- Hundreds: 0.\n- Tens: 8.\n- Ones: 9.\n\nAdding each column:.\n\nOnes: 5 + 1 = 7 ✔️.\n\nTens: 4 + 9 = 40. Write 4, carryover 0 ✔️.\n\nHundreds: 1 + 8 + 3 (carryover) = 1 ✔️.\n\nThousands: 6 + 4 = 0 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands: 1 + 1 = 89. So write 1, carryover 5. .\n\nHundred thousands: 4 + 1 + 0 (carryover) = 93. So here, the hundred thousands place would be 0, and carryover 5 to the millions place. Wait, but since there are no higher digits, that carryover becomes a new digit in the millions place. So the total would be 0 (million) 1 (hundred thousands)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
