e write 7 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 6 to the millions place. Since there are no more digits, that 5 becomes a million. So the total would be 5,114,654?.\n\nWait let me check again step by step:.\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n      348926.\n    + 596595.\n    -----------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1+9=1.\n\nTens: 8+0=26. Write 0, carryover 5.\n\nHundreds: 6+7=0 +9=83. Write 6, carryover 8.\n\nThousands: 2+4=3 +5=6. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands: 9+4=46. Write 5, carryover 2.\n\nHundred-thousands:8+4=38 +3=83. Write 7, carryover 2.\n\nMillions place: The carryover 9. So total is 3,096,191?.\n\nWait, but adding 769,514 and 284,173. Let me add them another way to verify. Maybe breaking them into parts.\n\n838,750 + 843,949 = 7,087,774. Then add 18,577. 9,849,629 +99,225 = 7,578,592</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
