071,593? Wait, but the approximate calculation gave 1,071,493. Wait, discrepancy here.\n\nWait, let's do the exact addition:\n\n546556\n\n+524937\n\nStart with the units:\n\n6+7=13 → 3, carry 1\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9 → 9, no carry\n\nHundreds:6+9=15 →5, carry1\n\nThousands:4+4=8 +1=9 →9, no carry\n\nTen thousands:5+2=7 →7\n\nHundred thousands:5+5=10 →0, carry1\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nMillions place:1\n\nHundred thousands:0\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:9\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:3\n\nSo the number is 1,071,593? But wait, when I approximated, I got 1,071,493. Hmm, that's a difference of 100. Where is the mistake?\n\nWait let me compute 546,556 +524,937:\n\nLet me add 546,556 +524,937 step by step:\n\n546,556 + 500,000 = 1,046,556\n\nThen add 24,937 to that:\n\n1,046,556 +24,937:\n\n1,046,556 +20,000 =1,066,556\n\n1,066,556 +4,937 =1,071,493. So that's correct. So why is the digit breakdown giving 1,071,593?\n\nAh! I see the mistake in the digit breakdown. Let me redo the addition:\n\nLet me write it out vertically again:\n\n  546556\n\n+524937\n\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 6+7=13 →3, carryover1\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9 →9, carryover0\n\nHundreds:6+9=15 →5, carryover1\n\nThousands:4 (from first number) +4 (from second) =8 +1=9 →9, carryover0\n\nTen thousands:5+2=7 →7, carryover0\n\nHundred thousands:5+5=10 →0, carryover1\n\nMillions place: the carryover1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left (positions 1-7):\n\nPosition1:3\n\nPosition2:9\n\nPosition3:5\n\nPosition4:9\n\nPosition5:7\n\nPosition6:0\n\nPosition7:1\n\nSo when written left to right (millions to ones):\n\nPosition7:1 (millions)\n\nPosition6:0 (hundred thousands)\n\nPosition5:7 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition4:9 (thousands)\n\nPosition3:5 (hundreds)\n\nPosition2:9 (tens)\n\nPosition1:3 (ones)\n\nSo the number is 1,079,593? Wait that's 1,079,593. But the approximate was 1,071,493. Now this is conflicting. There's a mistake here.\n\nWait, perhaps I added the thousands place incorrectly. Let me 