s no higher place, the 8 is added as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right: 3 (ones), 9 (tens), 6 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 4 (ten-thousands), then 25 in the hundred thousands. Wait, no, let me retrace. Wait, maybe I messed up the order of the places. Let me recount each step carefully.\n\nWait, perhaps I should list each digit's place step by step again to make sure:.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned properly:.\n\n      9 9 5 9 0 9.\n    + 6 5 6 4 1 7.\n    ---------------.\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 5 +4 =2. Write 3.\n\nTens:4 +1=56. Write 1, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds:6 +9=5, plus the carried 2 makes 7. Write 9.\n\nThousands:8 +4=1. Write 7.\n\nTen-thousands:3 +4=44. Write 0, carryover 3.\n\nHundred-thousands:2 +9=72, plus the carried 7 makes 75. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 0 (from first number) plus 9 (second number) is 28, plus the carried 5 is 97. So the hundred-thousands place is 9, and carryover 0 to the millions place. So the total would be 0 (million) 7 (hundred thousand), etc</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
