't mix up the places. Maybe I should write each digit's place explicitly.\n\nLet me list each digit position:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\nFirst number: 3.\nSecond number: 7.\nTotal: 1 + 0 = 25. Write 4, carryover 3.\n\nTens place:.\nFirst number: 3.\nSecond number: 5.\nPlus carryover 0: 1 + 8 + 5 = 1. Write 0, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place:.\nFirst number: 1.\nSecond number: 5.\nTotal: 9 + 3 = 84. Write 1, carryover 6.\n\nThousands place:.\nFirst number: 8.\nSecond number: 6.\nPlus carryover 7: 7 + 2 + 0 = 5. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nTen-thousands place:.\nFirst number: 1.\nSecond number: 7.\nTotal: 5 + 7 = 3. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:.\nFirst number: 4.\nSecond number: 1.\nTotal: 5 + 0 = 3. Write 9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
