nd has a 0. Adding those: 6 +1 =32. So that's 4 and 8, meaning 55. So we write 0 in the hundred thousands place and carry over another 5, but since there are no more digits, that 4 becomes a new digit at the beginning. Wait, but actually, both numbers only have up to the hundred thousands place. Wait, 034638 is a six-digit number, so 5 is in the hundred thousands place. The second number is 031,018, which is also six digits, so 1 in the hundred thousands. Adding 4 +3 gives 38, so we write 2 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 0 to the millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
