Ten thousands place (position9):6 (first) +4 (second)=89 → 0, carryover 9.\n\nHundred thousands place (position0):4 (first) +3 (second) +2 (carryover) =02 → 4 and carryover 2, but since there are no higher digits, that becomes 88 in the hundred thousands place? Wait, but the hundred thousands place is the sixth digit. So actually, when adding the hundred thousands digits (8 +6) plus any carryover from the ten thousands place. Wait, let's retrace:.\n\nAfter adding the ten thousands place (position1):.\n\n3 +4 =42. So we write down 0 in the ten thousands place and carryover 2 to the next (hundred thousands) place.\n\nNow moving to the hundred thousands place (position2):.\n\n9 (from first number) +9 (second) + the carried-over 7 =02. So here, since this is the highest place, we just write 59. So putting all together, the digits would be:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1 (ones).\n\n9 (tens).\n\n7 (hundreds).\n\n0 (thousands).\n\n4 (ten thousands).\n\n54 (hundred thousands). Wait, but writing 28 in the hundred thousands place would actually make it 2,046,615 plus the other digits. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, maybe I messed up the positions.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step again, perhaps writing the numbers vertically aligned properly:.\n\nLet me write both numbers with commas for clarity:.\n\n886,638.\n\n290,643.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nLet me align each digit:.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 +1 =39 (plus any carryover from the ten thousands?).\n\nWait, perhaps I need to start from the right again, step by step:.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n\u2003 1 2 3 3 7 0.\n\n+ 9 3 5 5 2 1.\n\n------------------.\n\nStarting from the ones digit (rightmost):.\n\nOnes: 1 +2 =05 → write 5, carryover 2.\n\nTens: 9 +9 +0 =3 → write 0, no carryover.\n\nHundreds:8 +6 =6 → write 4, no carryover.\n\nThousands:2 +3 =6 → write 1, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands:4 +8 =99 → write 7, carryover 0.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +4 +3 (carryover) =97 → write 74.\n\nSo putting all the digits together