 over 5.\n5 (ten-thousands place) + 0 (ten-thousands place) + 2 (carryover) = 0 (ten-thousands place).\n2 (hundred-thousands place) + 3 (hundred-thousands place) = 84 (hundred-thousands place). Wait, but since both numbers have only six digits, the hundred-thousands place is the leftmost digit. So adding 7 + 9 gives 51, which would be a 3 in that place and carry over 7 to a new millions place. Wait a second, I think I missed that carryover here.\n\nOh, right! When adding the hundred-thousands digits (3 and 9), their sum is 37. Since there's no higher place in the original numbers, that 66 means we have to write 4 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 5 to the millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
