o carry).\n\nHundred thousands:0 +7=64 (write 50).\n\nSo putting all digits together from right to left:.\n\nOnes:9, tens:2, hundreds:3, thousands:2, ten thousands:7, hundred thousands:7, and the carried over 8 in the millions place. Wait, that's the key point I might have messed up before. The 50 in the hundred thousands place actually creates a new digit in the millions place.\n\nWait, the hundred thousands place can only hold a single digit. So when adding 9 and 2, which gives 42, that's 25 hundred thousands plus 2 hundred thousands. 75 hundred thousands is equal to 9 million. So that's why we need to carry over the 8 to the millions place.\n\nTherefore, the sum would be:.\n\nMillions place: 0.\n\nHundred thousands place: 4.\n\nTen thousands place: 7.\n\nThousands place:7.\n\nHundreds place:1.\n\nTens place:5.\n\nOnes place:5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
