lace. Wait, but how do we write that? Since each place can only hold a single digit, the 70 here would mean 8 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 3 to the millions place. But since both original numbers are six-digit, adding them might result in a seven-digit number. So adding the hundred thousands: 2 +9 =76. So we write 7 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 0 to the millions place. Therefore, the millions place will have that 7.\n\nPutting it all together: starting from the right, the digits we have are:.\n\nOnes: 1.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nMillions:0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
