final_output:  ['1,301,132. Wait, that doesn\'t seem right. Let me check again.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the carrying over. Let me try again step by step.\n\nWait, actually the numbers were 398615 and 255619. Let me correct that. The original problem is 398,615 plus 255,619.\n\nStarting over:\n\nAlign the numbers:\n\n398615\n+255619\n----------\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\n5 + 9 = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n\nTens place: 1 + 1 = 2, plus the carried 1 makes 3. Wait, wait: the tens digits are 1 and 1. Wait, let\'s break it down properly:\n\nOnes: 5 +9 =14 (4, carry 1)\nTens: 1 (from 398,615\'s tens place) plus 1 (from 255,619\'s tens) plus 1 carried = 3. So write 3, no carryover.\n\nHundreds place: 6 (from first number) and 6 (second): 6+6=12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 8 (from first) and 5 (second) plus carried 1: 8+5=13, plus 1 is 14. So write 4 and carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 9 (first number) and 5 (second): 9+5=14 plus carried 1 is 15. Write 5 and carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 3 +2 =5 plus carried 1 is 6. So writing all together: 654,234? Wait, let\'s see:\n\nWait the digits step by step:\n\nLet me write each digit\'s positions:\n\nNumbers:\n\n398,615\n+255,619\n------------\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (ones to hundred-thousands):\n\nOnes:\n5 (from 398615) + 9 (from 255619) =14 → 4, carryover 1\n\nTens:\n1 (from 398615\'s tens) + 1 (from 255619\'s tens) = 2, plus carryover 1 → 3 → 3, no carryover\n\nHundreds:\n6 (from 398615\'s hundreds) +6 (from 255619\'s hundreds) =12 → 2, carryover 1\n\nThousands:\n8 (398615\'s thousands) +5 (255619\'s thousands) =13 + carryover 1 →14 →4, carryover1\n\nTen-thousands:\n9 (398615\'s ten-thousands digit) +5 (255619\'s ten-thousands) =14 + carryover1 →15 →5, carryover1\n\nHundred-thousands:\n3 (398615\'s hundred-thousands) +2 (255619\'s hundred-thousands) =5 + carryover1 →6 →6, no carryover.\n\nSo putting all together: 6 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 4 (