, carry over 2.\n\nTens: 1 + 4 = 7, plus 2 carried over is 8. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nHundreds: 2 + 5 = 7. Write 3.\n\nThousands: 8 + 5 = 1. Write 3.\n\nTen-thousands: 3 (from 241,373) and 2 (from 522,349). Wait, actually, let's see:.\n\nWait, hold on, maybe I misaligned the digits. Let me check the place values again. Let's break down each number into their digits:.\n\n706,286 is:.\n\n- Hundred thousands: 4.\n- Ten thousands: 2.\n- Thousands: 0.\n- Hundreds: 3.\n- Tens: 8.\n- Ones: 1.\n\n081,993 is:.\n\n- Hundred thousands: 7.\n- Ten thousands: 1.\n- Thousands: 9.\n- Hundreds: 6.\n- Tens: 1.\n- Ones: 9.\n\nSo when adding, the places are:.\n\nOnes: 4 +4 =76 ✔️.\n\nTens:1+5=6 +3=2 ✔️.\n\nHundreds:6+5=7 ✔️.\n\nThousands:8 +9=6 ✔️.\n\nTen thousands:4 +8=4 ✔️.\n\nHundred thousands:6 +5=86. .\n\nSo the hundred thousands place adds to 97. That means we have to carry over again. Because 81 in the hundred thousands place would actually be 0,272,243 plus 6 in the hundred thousands. Wait, right, so when you have 61 in the hundred thousands place, that's equivalent to 8 million and 5 in the hundred thousands. So we need to add a new digit to the left for the millions place. .\n\nSo the total would be 0 (million) 3 (hundred thousands), and then the rest. .\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we've got are:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:4.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nHundred thousands:9 (since 99 was carried over to the millions place).\n\nMillions place:4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
