nTens: 7.\nHundreds: 8.\nThousands: 8.\nTen thousands: 9.\nHundred thousands: 0.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:.\n\n```.\n      1 5 8 9 4 9.\n    + 4 3 3 3 9 2.\n    ---------------.\n```.\n\nWait, actually, perhaps it's better to align each digit vertically. Let me write each digit's place:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 0 + 8 = 5 (as before). .\n\nTens: 1 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 83. Oh, wait, that's 69. So here we have to carry over. The sum here is 03, so we write down 2 and carry over 7 to the next column (hundreds place).\n\nHundreds place: 2 (from first) + 0 (from second) plus the carried over 3. So 8+8=68, plus 4 is 36. So we put 1 here and carry over 2 again.\n\nThousands place: 5 (first number) + 8 (second number) plus the carried over 2. 9+2=88 +7=78. Again, write 7 and carry over 7.\n\nTen thousands place: 8 (from first number) + 0 (from second number) plus the carried over 8. That's 0+6+4=7. So 6 here, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 (from first) +1 (from second) =39. So that's 55. Since there are no more digits, we just write 48.\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nTens:2 (with carryover 8).\n\nHundreds:7 (with carryover 2).\n\nThousands:7 (with carryover 4).\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nHundred thousands:31.\n\nWait, but when we write the total sum, the hundred thousands place is 38, so that would actually be 4,1 in the hundred thousands and ten thousands? Wait, no, maybe I messed up the places.\n\nWait, let me go through each step again carefully.\n\nLet me write each digit vertically aligned:.\n\nLet me write the numbers as:.\n\nFirst number: 582,737 is:.\n\nHundred thousands:8, Ten thousands:8, Thousands:7, Hundreds:4, Tens:3, Ones:9.\n\nSecond number: 148,070 is:.\n\nHundred thousands:9, Ten thousands:2, Thousands:7, Hundreds:1, Tens:2, Ones:9.\n\nSo adding vertically:.\n\nStarting from the right (Ones):.\n\nOnes: 9 + 1 =4. Write down 5.\n\nTens: 3 +7 =22. Write 4, carryover 4.\n\nHundreds:8 +5 =00, plus 7 carried over is 41. Write 5, carryover 4.\n\nThousands:5 +0 =83, plus 7 =36. Write 7, carryover 6.\n\nTen thousands:5 +8 =8, plus 5 carried over =2. Write 6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:4 +0 =37. Write 28.\n\nSo putting all digits together:.\n\nThe result is 78 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
