undreds:0+0+3=68 ✔️  .\nThousands:3+6+3=44 ✔️  .\nTen-thousands:2+0+0=60 ✔️  .\nHundred-thousands:5+4+2=67 ✔️  .\n\nSo the digits from right to left would be 4 (ones), 9 (tens), 0 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 0 (ten-thousands), 0 (hundred-thousands) plus the final carryover 7. Wait, actually, when we add the hundred-thousands place, we get 39, so that's 0 in the hundred-thousands place and carryover 8. Then that becomes the next digit</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
