 the right:.\n\nOnes: 4 + 1 = 1.\n\nTens: 3 + 1 = 1.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 6 = 88. Write down 3, carryover 6.\n\nThousands: 4 (from first number) + 5 (from second) plus the carryover 3 makes 4. So 4.\n\nTen thousands: 8 (from first) + 4 (from second) = 3.\n\nHundred thousands: 5 (from first) + 5 (from second) = 8.\n\nSo combining all digits: 3 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
