ndreds), 0 (tens), 2 (ones).\n\n301,913 is also 0 digits: 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo when adding, each column is:.\n\nOnes: 7 +1 =06 → 1 carry 8.\n\nTens:7 +6 +9=92 →9 carry 4.\n\nHundreds:6 +5 +2=3 → no carry.\n\nThousands:0 +7=2.\n\nTen thousands:9 +3=1.\n\nHundred thousands:6+1=0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
