e it clearer:.\n\n647,356 is:.\n\n1 (hundred thousands).\n7 (ten thousands).\n0 (thousands).\n3 (hundreds).\n0 (tens).\n0 (ones).\n\n194,164 is:.\n\n0 (hundred thousands).\n9 (ten thousands).\n8 (thousands).\n0 (hundreds).\n1 (tens).\n4 (ones).\n\nSo when adding vertically, align each column:.\n\nLet me write them out vertically:.\n\n      2 4 2 4 6 5.\n    + 7 5 0 7 1 0.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 4 +8 =98. Write 9, carryover 0.\n\nTens: 8 +9 =96, plus 6 is 79. Write 1, carryover 2.\n\nHundreds:9 +4 =3, plus 8 is 4. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:6 (from first number) +7 (from second) =3. So 5, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:3 (first number) +2 (second) =91. Write 1, carryover 7.\n\nHundred thousands place:5 +2 =45, plus the carried-over 3 makes 24. So write 6 and carryover 3, but since there's no higher place, that 4 becomes a new digit.\n\nWait, let me check each step again step by step to avoid mistakes.\n\nLet me do each digit step by step:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n0. Ones place: 6 + 7 = 60. So write down 1, carry over 7.\n\n1. Tens place: 8 (from first number) + 5 (from second) = 58, plus the carried 7 makes 21. So write 2, carry over 5.\n\n4. Hundreds place: 8 + 9 =8, plus 8 carried over is 3. Write 4, no carryover.\n\n2. Thousands place: 7 (from first number) +0 (from second number) =3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\n3. Ten thousands place: 7 (from first number) +3 (from second number) =89. Write 6, carry over 0.\n\n8. Hundred thousands place: 2 (from first number) +4 (from second number) =40, plus the carried 3 is 86. So write 6 and carry over 0. But since there are no more digits, that carried 2 becomes the next digit (millions place).\n\nPutting it all together, the digits from right to left are:.\n\nOnes: 9.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nPlus the carried-over 3 in the millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
