), 1 (hundreds), 0 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), and 6 (hundred thousands). Wait a second, let me check again because when I added the ten-thousands place, was that correct?.\n\nWait, let me go through each step again carefully to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me write them aligned:.\n\n      9 0 3 4 9 8.\n    + 5 7 1 8 2 1.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 1 + 7 = 20. Write 6, carryover 8. Correct.\n\nTens: 4 + 5 = 0, plus the 5 carried over is 0. So 2. Good.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 0 = 2. So 1. .\n\nThousands: 4 (from first number) + 9 (from second number) = 9. .\n\nTen-thousands: 5 (from first) + 3 (from second) = 1. .\n\nHundred-thousands: 3 + 9 = 9. .\n\nSo combining all the digits: 2 (hundred-thousands), 5 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 6 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
