k that again.\n\nWait a second, maybe I made a mistake in the thousands place. Let me go through each step again carefully.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n\u2003745,970.\n+806,693.\n----------.\n\nBreaking it down by place:.\n\nOnes place: 1 + 6 = 5 (correct).\n\nTens place: 6 + 0 = 2 (correct).\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 8 = 8 (correct).\n\nThousands place: 1 (from 223,082) + 3 (from 687,654) = 52. So we write 9 and carry over 7 to the next (ten thousands) place.\n\nTen thousands place: 2 (from first number) + 5 (from second number) + 5 (carryover) = 26. So again, we write 9 here and carry over 7 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 + 7 + 5 (carryover) = 0. .\n\nSo putting all the digits together from right to left: .\n\nOnes:5, Tens:2, Hundreds:6, Thousands:5, Ten thousands:5, Hundred thousands:3</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
