28 + 391,160:\n\n409,828 + 391,160\n\nAdd the thousands: 409,000 + 391,000 = 800,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 828 + 160 = 988.\n\nTotal is 800,000 + 988 = 800,988. So that matches the previous result. But let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, let's add digit by digit step-by-step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8\n\nTens: 2 + 6 = 8\n\nHundreds: 8 + 1 = 9\n\nThousands: 9 (from first) + 1 (from second) = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands: 0 (from first) + 9 (from second) + 1 (carryover) = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 4 + 3 + 1 (carryover) = 8.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:0,\n\nThousands:0,\n\nHundreds:9,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo the sum is 800,988. That seems correct. So the answer should be 800,988.\n\nWait, but in my first calculation when I thought of 745,970 and 806,693, which were different numbers, I got confused, but now focusing on the problem's numbers, 409,828 and 391,160, the correct sum is 800,988.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another approach. Let's add them numerically:\n\n409,828\n\n+391,160\n\n= ?\n\n400,000 + 300,000 = 700,000\n\n9,000 + 90,000 = 99,000 \u2192 Wait, no. Breaking down each number:\n\nFirst number: 400,000 + 9,000 + 800 + 20 +8\n\nSecond number: 300,000 + 90,000 + 1,000 + 100 + 60 +0\n\nAdding each part:\n\n400k + 300k =700k\n\n9k +90k =99k\n\n1k (from second) \u2192 total so far 700k+99k+1k = 800k?\n\nWait, perhaps this is complicating. Let me do it step by step:\n\n409,828\n\n+391,160\n\nAdd the two numbers:\n\nStart from right:\n\n8+0=8\n\n2+6=8\n\n8+1=9\n\n9 (thousands place) +1 (thousands place) =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\n0 (ten thousands) +9 (ten thousands) +1 carried =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1.\n\n4 (hundred thousands) +3 (hundred thousands) +1 carried =8.\n\nSo the digits are 8 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones). So 800,988. Yes, that's correct