rting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 6 +4 =0.\n\nTens:0 +8=5.\n\nHundreds:8 +6=4.\n\nThousands:6 +7=6.\n\nTen thousands:8 +3=55 (so 6 here, carryover 8).\n\nHundred thousands:4 +7 +0(carry)=0.\n\nSo combining all digits: 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 2 (ones). Wait, no, wait. Wait, the thousands place was 4+9=5, so thousands digit is 8. Then the ten thousands was 2+8=60, so ten thousands is 7 with carryover. Then the hundred thousands is 2+1+0=6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
